WEBVTT

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:09.926
A NETFLIX SERIES

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:22.689
KOTARO LIVES ALONE

00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:12.447
OHBA DENTISTRY

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:14.741
At Ohba Dentistry, where I work,

00:01:14.824 --> 00:01:18.745
we take one hour for children's exams,
double the time for adult exams.

00:01:18.828 --> 00:01:22.457
What? You say I have to put up with
the pain until then?

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:23.500
I've had enough!

00:01:25.668 --> 00:01:27.670
This is happening again…

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.798
Do you have a minute, Namie?

00:01:30.507 --> 00:01:33.093
Oh, good to see you, Dr. Ohba.

00:01:33.176 --> 00:01:35.762
Could you tell me the schedule
for the rest of the day?

00:01:37.305 --> 00:01:38.807
Doctor!

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:39.766
What is it?

00:01:39.849 --> 00:01:43.520
Can we please make
the children's exam times a bit shorter?

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:44.604
- No.
- Huh?

00:01:45.146 --> 00:01:49.275
What are you doing with all that
extra time with the children?

00:01:49.359 --> 00:01:50.527
Chatting.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:53.113
What?

00:01:53.196 --> 00:01:54.114
Chatting.

00:01:55.824 --> 00:01:56.825
I don't get it.

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.453
Good day to you.

00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:04.332
Hello, Kotaro.
You're right on time as usual.

00:02:04.415 --> 00:02:07.961
Yes. I am Mr. Right on Time.

00:02:08.044 --> 00:02:10.421
30 MINUTES LATER

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:15.176
I'll get to the bottom of
this "chatting" business today!

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.387
Are you enjoying kindergarten lately?

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.055
- Yes.
- You eating three meals a day?

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.808
It sounds more like
a witness interview than chatting!

00:02:21.891 --> 00:02:24.936
Yes. This morning, I put egg in my natto.

00:02:25.603 --> 00:02:26.813
Yes. I see.

00:02:26.896 --> 00:02:29.440
I don't get it after all.

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:32.694
Okay. Well, see you again next week.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:35.488
Yes. See you again later.

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:41.161
Come to think of it,

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:44.414
why did Kotaro have so many cavities
at the beginning?

00:02:44.914 --> 00:02:47.083
You were just eavesdropping, right?

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:50.211
Well, Doctor, I wondered why

00:02:50.295 --> 00:02:53.590
you were making time
to chat with the kids.

00:02:54.966 --> 00:02:58.178
I didn't have time for that before.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:00.013
Then, why?

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.475
Konoe, come on in.

00:03:05.602 --> 00:03:07.687
Alright. Open your mouth, please.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:13.568
Huh? More than half her teeth
have cavities, and most are serious.

00:03:13.651 --> 00:03:16.070
How did she tolerate this until now?

00:03:18.072 --> 00:03:21.201
Seriously. What are
this child's parents doing?

00:03:26.247 --> 00:03:28.249
The next appointment is in 4 to 5 days.

00:03:28.917 --> 00:03:30.460
Tell your mother that,

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:33.421
"The dentist says
to brush your teeth properly."

00:03:37.675 --> 00:03:40.720
Doctor, Konoe just rushed into the office,

00:03:40.803 --> 00:03:42.931
saying that her teeth hurt.

00:03:43.014 --> 00:03:45.183
But our appointments are full today…

00:03:45.266 --> 00:03:49.604
I believe that child has an appointment
first thing tomorrow, so

00:03:49.687 --> 00:03:52.774
let's give her the painkillers
I prescribed earlier today,

00:03:52.857 --> 00:03:56.277
and tell her to come with her mom
to the appointed time tomorrow.

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:05.745
In the end, Konoe never came back
to the dentist's office.

00:04:05.828 --> 00:04:08.081
What? Why?

00:04:17.215 --> 00:04:19.467
EMACIATED FEMALE CHILD
TAKEN INTO CUSTODY

00:04:20.635 --> 00:04:23.221
The kid in this article was Konoe?!

00:04:23.304 --> 00:04:26.557
Yes. I should have noticed earlier

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:32.480
when I found
such an abnormal amount of cavities.

00:04:33.523 --> 00:04:37.193
Is that why
Kotaro had so many cavities too?

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:38.111
Yes.

00:04:38.736 --> 00:04:43.032
However, it seems like he's now
been able to get away from that situation.

00:04:44.826 --> 00:04:46.327
Children's cavities

00:04:46.411 --> 00:04:49.831
can sometimes be a sign of
a cry for help that no one else can hear.

00:04:51.916 --> 00:04:56.212
I don't want to miss
hearing that cry again.

00:04:57.213 --> 00:04:59.507
So that's why you chat.

00:05:02.176 --> 00:05:04.137
Yes, this is Ohba Dentistry.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:06.514
Yes. An appointment for your child?

00:05:06.597 --> 00:05:11.853
At our office, we take one full hour
for children's exams.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:19.736
It's still raining.

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:21.487
Well, if it isn't Ms. Takei.

00:05:21.571 --> 00:05:24.699
You must be coming home from work.
You must be tired.

00:05:24.782 --> 00:05:26.451
Yes.

00:05:26.534 --> 00:05:30.621
What are you doing? What is that sign?

00:05:30.705 --> 00:05:34.250
A rainy-day tradition.
It is the Umbrella Share Service.

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:36.586
Umbrella Share Service?

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:42.050
Yes. My Umbrella Share Service
is a fine skill taught to me by my master.

00:05:42.133 --> 00:05:43.051
Master?

00:05:43.134 --> 00:05:45.219
What do you think?
Would you like to come under?

00:05:45.303 --> 00:05:48.431
No! I'm fine! I have my own umbrella.

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:54.062
That's right, being close to me
is torture for you, Ms. Takei.

00:05:54.145 --> 00:05:55.146
My apologies.

00:05:55.229 --> 00:05:57.690
No, it's not torture.

00:05:57.774 --> 00:06:01.611
It's not as if I'm bad with kids!

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:03.196
Oh, Kotaro!

00:06:03.279 --> 00:06:06.115
Could you share your umbrella with me
to the usual place?

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:07.450
I'd like to go next.

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:09.285
I want it as well.

00:06:09.369 --> 00:06:11.371
- Me too!
- And me!

00:06:11.454 --> 00:06:12.914
Yes, we will go in order.

00:06:12.997 --> 00:06:14.707
It's surprisingly popular?!

00:06:14.791 --> 00:06:17.668
ANOTHER DAY

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:23.341
He said it was a rainy-day tradition,

00:06:23.424 --> 00:06:25.760
but he really is doing it every time.

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:30.431
Kotaro,

00:06:30.515 --> 00:06:33.726
that shoulder is being rained on.
Are you okay?

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:35.728
It is nothing to worry about.

00:06:35.812 --> 00:06:40.024
My master taught me this is what it means
to be a professional umbrella sharer.

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:42.568
Thank you!

00:06:47.031 --> 00:06:48.366
Sir Boyfriend!

00:06:48.449 --> 00:06:52.787
Do you not see that your umbrella sharing
is getting your girlfriend's shoulder wet?

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:55.164
Oh, sorry! I didn't notice.

00:06:55.248 --> 00:06:56.541
Oh, I'm fine.

00:06:58.793 --> 00:07:01.170
Would you like to get under my umbrella?

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:03.464
I will protect you from the rain.

00:07:03.548 --> 00:07:05.133
- Okay!
- Huh?

00:07:05.216 --> 00:07:06.926
Umbrella Sharing Prince!

00:07:07.009 --> 00:07:09.971
You should look at how wet my shoulder is.

00:07:10.054 --> 00:07:12.265
He really is proud of that.

00:07:12.348 --> 00:07:15.351
Even so, he sure is
obsessed with his shoulder.

00:07:19.647 --> 00:07:22.900
Hello, Lady Takei.
Another tough day at work, I see.

00:07:22.984 --> 00:07:25.236
Hey, your shoulder is soaking wet!

00:07:25.319 --> 00:07:28.072
It is my proof
of being an umbrella sharer.

00:07:28.156 --> 00:07:30.533
I am sure my master would be proud.

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:34.036
"Master" again. Who is this "Master"?

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:38.249
Kotaro, why are you so intent
about sharing your umbrella

00:07:38.332 --> 00:07:40.418
and getting your shoulder wet?

00:07:43.129 --> 00:07:46.257
A long time ago, one rainy day,

00:07:46.340 --> 00:07:48.301
my master and I were going home…

00:07:49.886 --> 00:07:51.637
Maybe his master is…

00:08:04.066 --> 00:08:06.319
You're getting wet! Your shoulder!

00:08:06.402 --> 00:08:08.863
Oh, Daddy's fine.

00:08:08.946 --> 00:08:12.700
I know. Let me teach you something
important about sharing an umbrella.

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:14.410
Important?

00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:17.413
It's to hold an umbrella
in consideration of the person.

00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:20.124
The proof is that your shoulder gets wet.

00:08:21.876 --> 00:08:24.712
Amazing, you're a pro!
An umbrella sharing pro!

00:08:24.795 --> 00:08:26.464
Wow! Amazing!

00:08:44.565 --> 00:08:47.777
Some day, when I share an umbrella
with my parents,

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:50.571
I'll be able to show them my wet shoulder.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:56.702
You're right. Then your feelings
will be communicated.

00:08:58.329 --> 00:09:02.583
Hey, can I ask you to share your umbrella
with me today as well?

00:09:02.667 --> 00:09:05.628
Huh? What a surprise.
Are you feeling quite well?

00:09:05.711 --> 00:09:07.797
What? I'm fine.

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:10.216
Then, please come on in.

00:09:12.468 --> 00:09:15.388
I'll hold the umbrella.

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:18.474
What are you saying? I will hold it.

00:09:18.558 --> 00:09:20.685
Why not? Just this once.

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:24.730
Your face is covered in sweat.

00:09:24.814 --> 00:09:26.899
It's just your imagination.

00:09:31.112 --> 00:09:35.324
Lady Takei, next time
let me hold the umbrella.

00:09:35.825 --> 00:09:38.369
I'll look forward to it.

00:09:40.329 --> 00:09:42.540
THOSE WHO ARE WELCOME/MEMORY OF A PILLOW

00:09:42.623 --> 00:09:46.002
Banana in curry?
That's not a thing, right?

00:09:46.085 --> 00:09:47.628
Banana can't go in curry.

00:09:48.504 --> 00:09:51.841
In that case, I shall deliver
my homemade curry to you.

00:09:51.924 --> 00:09:53.050
You should try it.

00:09:53.134 --> 00:09:55.136
Game on. Give it your best shot.

00:09:55.219 --> 00:09:57.346
Lucky me! I get a free meal.

00:09:57.430 --> 00:10:00.016
I found you! I've been watching.

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:06.897
'Sup? It's been a while. Welcome!

00:10:10.067 --> 00:10:12.820
Let's hurry home. If your eyes meet,
you'll turn to stone--

00:10:12.903 --> 00:10:14.405
- Sir Tasuku.
- Huh?

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:18.284
Is it not Sir Tasuku?

00:10:18.367 --> 00:10:21.996
Yo! You been good, Kotaro?
All right, let's go!

00:10:22.079 --> 00:10:24.749
Three, two, one!

00:10:26.584 --> 00:10:29.295
Woo! You're the best Kotaro! Woo!

00:10:29.378 --> 00:10:31.005
Sir Tasuku! Woo!

00:10:31.088 --> 00:10:32.632
You know him?

00:10:32.715 --> 00:10:35.009
Sir Tasuku was in the orphanage with me!

00:10:35.092 --> 00:10:37.553
I'm working as a host now! Yeah!

00:10:37.637 --> 00:10:40.640
Sir Tasuku, come up to my room!

00:10:40.723 --> 00:10:42.558
Thank you, you are welcome!

00:10:42.642 --> 00:10:45.353
Sir Karino, we will have curry next time!

00:10:45.436 --> 00:10:46.771
Sir Tasuku! Woo!

00:10:46.854 --> 00:10:49.440
You guys must have been
buddy-buddy before.

00:10:51.484 --> 00:10:54.070
I ran into Ryota the other day!

00:10:54.153 --> 00:10:58.366
When I heard about you from him,
I wanted to see you too, so I came.

00:10:58.449 --> 00:10:59.700
I meet you!

00:10:59.784 --> 00:11:02.745
That makes me glad. Thank you, Sir Tasuku!

00:11:03.913 --> 00:11:07.500
Hey, do you spend a lot of time
with that guy from earlier?

00:11:07.583 --> 00:11:10.711
Sir Karino? He's my neighbor.

00:11:10.795 --> 00:11:13.255
He takes me to and from kindergarten,

00:11:13.339 --> 00:11:16.092
goes shopping with me,
and spends a lot of time with me.

00:11:17.009 --> 00:11:17.843
Don't…

00:11:18.386 --> 00:11:19.220
Hmm?

00:11:19.804 --> 00:11:21.389
…let your guard down too much.

00:11:23.391 --> 00:11:24.892
Bon appétit!

00:11:27.812 --> 00:11:29.814
It's really delicious!

00:11:29.897 --> 00:11:33.275
I remember the orphanage
served curry a lot too. Hot!

00:11:33.359 --> 00:11:35.653
Yes. I remember that.

00:11:37.071 --> 00:11:39.532
The way you mix and eat is as I remember.

00:11:39.615 --> 00:11:44.036
You're so sloppy mixing it too. Oh no!

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:45.830
Hey, give it to me. Here.

00:11:45.913 --> 00:11:47.331
Oh, sorry.

00:11:49.458 --> 00:11:52.920
By the way, I heard you get a little money

00:11:53.003 --> 00:11:54.630
donated to you every week.

00:11:54.714 --> 00:11:55.548
Yes.

00:11:56.632 --> 00:11:59.885
So, I have a little favor to ask of you.

00:12:05.391 --> 00:12:06.308
Huh?!

00:12:06.851 --> 00:12:09.645
Oh, sorry. Are you okay?

00:12:09.729 --> 00:12:11.605
- Yes.
- You're…

00:12:13.441 --> 00:12:14.734
The belly dancing lawyer.

00:12:14.817 --> 00:12:16.068
I'm Kobayashi!

00:12:16.152 --> 00:12:21.407
Well, I'm here to give Kotaro
his living allowance,

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:25.453
but recently he's been continuously asking
to increase the amount.

00:12:25.536 --> 00:12:26.370
Huh?

00:12:26.871 --> 00:12:29.874
What's more, the amount is increasing.

00:12:29.957 --> 00:12:33.210
When I ask him,
he just says he needs more.

00:12:34.295 --> 00:12:37.173
Mr. Karino, can you think of anything?

00:12:37.715 --> 00:12:39.675
Something that's changed recently?

00:12:40.426 --> 00:12:41.385
Actually…

00:12:42.762 --> 00:12:44.764
A FEW DAYS LATER

00:12:45.681 --> 00:12:48.434
Okay, later Kotaro! Peace!

00:12:52.313 --> 00:12:53.147
Hmm?

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:56.066
Hey. Tasuku, isn't it?

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:57.943
There's something I wanna ask.

00:12:58.027 --> 00:13:00.070
What is it, old human?

00:13:00.154 --> 00:13:02.990
"Old"?! Well, yeah…

00:13:04.241 --> 00:13:08.662
Well, it seems you've been coming to
Kotaro's place a lot recently,

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:12.583
so I thought you'd know something
about his finances.

00:13:12.666 --> 00:13:13.501
Yeah.

00:13:13.584 --> 00:13:17.171
Kotaro and I
are planning on living together.

00:13:17.254 --> 00:13:18.464
Huh?

00:13:18.547 --> 00:13:21.842
So that's why I need money to move. Need!

00:13:21.926 --> 00:13:26.055
Yeah, but right now he's living
by himself to get stronger--

00:13:26.138 --> 00:13:29.892
Seems like you take care of
a few things for Kotaro, huh?

00:13:29.975 --> 00:13:32.895
But you're just a neighbor
in the same building.

00:13:32.978 --> 00:13:37.483
Since I grew up in the same situation
as Kotaro, I know him better than you,

00:13:37.566 --> 00:13:39.568
who just happens to be a neighbor.

00:13:42.446 --> 00:13:45.199
SIR RYOTA

00:13:46.742 --> 00:13:48.828
Sir Ryota. It is me.

00:13:48.911 --> 00:13:52.665
Hey, Kotaro.
I ran into Tasuku the other day,

00:13:52.748 --> 00:13:55.042
and when I talked about you
he wanted to see you.

00:13:55.125 --> 00:13:57.419
Yes. I saw him a moment ago.

00:13:57.503 --> 00:14:01.090
I see.
Considering the situation with your dad,

00:14:01.173 --> 00:14:03.676
I wasn't sure about sharing your address.

00:14:04.677 --> 00:14:07.137
But you got along
with Tasuku the best, right?

00:14:09.723 --> 00:14:12.142
So I thought seeing him
would make you happy.

00:14:12.226 --> 00:14:13.853
Thank you, Sir Ryota.

00:14:14.395 --> 00:14:18.274
It is no problem at all,
so you do not need to worry.

00:14:18.357 --> 00:14:20.484
Kotaro is going to move?

00:14:20.568 --> 00:14:24.655
According to Tasuku,
they are going to live together.

00:14:24.738 --> 00:14:28.868
He may be asking for more
living allowance for moving expenses.

00:14:28.951 --> 00:14:32.037
If he's moving, why didn't he tell me?

00:14:32.121 --> 00:14:35.374
It's also concerning that
the amounts are increasing.

00:14:36.917 --> 00:14:40.838
Just in case,
I will run a check on Tasuku.

00:14:42.214 --> 00:14:44.508
Borrowing the strength
of this lawyer badge!

00:14:44.592 --> 00:14:45.676
Okay.

00:14:46.218 --> 00:14:48.345
It must be some kind of mistake.

00:14:48.429 --> 00:14:53.100
Kotaro wouldn't leave you guys
and this apartment building.

00:14:53.183 --> 00:14:54.310
Maybe.

00:14:55.185 --> 00:14:56.478
But in the meantime…

00:15:00.691 --> 00:15:03.193
Hey, so…

00:15:03.277 --> 00:15:07.489
Is it true that you need money
to move in with Tasuku?

00:15:08.282 --> 00:15:09.783
Yes. That is true.

00:15:10.451 --> 00:15:11.285
Oh…

00:15:12.536 --> 00:15:14.038
Hmm, I see.

00:15:14.705 --> 00:15:17.499
I just came to confirm that. Later.

00:15:22.546 --> 00:15:25.549
I see. He really is moving out.

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:29.720
Tasuku must be that important to him…

00:15:33.015 --> 00:15:34.391
ORPHANAGE
SUN HOUSE

00:15:34.475 --> 00:15:38.145
This is Kotaro, who will join us
in the orphanage from today.

00:15:38.228 --> 00:15:39.772
Everyone, be friends with him!

00:15:39.855 --> 00:15:41.273
Okay!

00:15:46.987 --> 00:15:49.406
Hey! You can't do that, Kotaro!

00:15:50.032 --> 00:15:53.369
Seriously, what are you doing?
Stop making a mess!

00:15:54.370 --> 00:15:55.871
It's all torn up.

00:15:58.415 --> 00:16:00.417
Looks like you're having tons of fun!

00:16:00.501 --> 00:16:02.962
Let me join you. Enjoy!

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:06.423
Wow, I'm into it!

00:16:06.507 --> 00:16:10.219
Amazing, Kotaro. What a great find! Woo!

00:16:10.302 --> 00:16:12.596
Tasuku started doing it too!

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:15.557
I'll clean up
and Ryota will fix the pillow later.

00:16:15.641 --> 00:16:17.726
It's all good. Okay!

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:18.727
Why me? Hey.

00:16:18.811 --> 00:16:21.730
It's a cotton party for everyone. Woo!

00:16:22.648 --> 00:16:24.274
Haha!

00:16:24.358 --> 00:16:25.776
I'll do it too!

00:16:25.859 --> 00:16:26.694
All right, get in!

00:16:35.661 --> 00:16:39.748
Kotaro sure is different
from when he first arrived.

00:16:39.832 --> 00:16:43.419
You're right, he's friendly with everyone
and is talking!

00:16:43.502 --> 00:16:46.046
- Might be thanks to you, Tasuku.
- Me?

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:48.424
When Kotaro first came here,

00:16:48.507 --> 00:16:51.927
you joined him taking cotton
out of a pillow, right?

00:16:52.011 --> 00:16:54.555
Oh, yeah. I did that, didn't I?

00:16:54.638 --> 00:16:59.601
That time, I think Kotaro was really happy
that you accepted him

00:17:00.227 --> 00:17:02.479
and didn't reject him.

00:17:02.563 --> 00:17:06.025
That's what got him to start opening up.

00:17:06.108 --> 00:17:08.360
You exaggerate, mister.

00:17:08.444 --> 00:17:11.739
When he was pulling out the cotton,
it just seemed to me

00:17:11.822 --> 00:17:15.492
like he was saying,
"somebody pay attention to me!"

00:17:19.621 --> 00:17:20.456
It's gone!

00:17:21.915 --> 00:17:23.459
What's wrong?

00:17:23.959 --> 00:17:25.711
My wallet is gone!

00:17:26.295 --> 00:17:29.840
It was Tasuku, right? You stole my wallet!

00:17:29.923 --> 00:17:31.341
Haha, that's awful.

00:17:32.509 --> 00:17:34.720
Ah, it's Tasuku.

00:17:34.803 --> 00:17:36.555
He wouldn't hesitate.

00:17:37.347 --> 00:17:39.600
- Sir Tasuku would not do that!
- Huh?

00:17:39.683 --> 00:17:42.936
I will help out,
so could you search one more time?

00:17:46.273 --> 00:17:49.234
I am glad the wallet was found.

00:17:49.318 --> 00:17:50.152
Yeah.

00:17:50.235 --> 00:17:53.739
And thank you very much
for standing up for me earlier!

00:17:54.656 --> 00:17:57.868
I was arrested for shoplifting before,

00:17:57.951 --> 00:18:00.621
so they suspect me, okay?

00:18:00.704 --> 00:18:03.123
- The past does not matter.
- Oh?

00:18:03.207 --> 00:18:05.459
I believe in you, Tasuku.

00:18:09.254 --> 00:18:12.299
You believe in people too easily, Kotaro.

00:18:16.804 --> 00:18:18.555
Did something happen?

00:18:19.681 --> 00:18:24.019
Tasuku is in debt
with several consumer loans,

00:18:24.103 --> 00:18:26.355
and had fallen quite behind in payments,

00:18:27.022 --> 00:18:30.442
but it seems he's recently begun
to slowly pay them back.

00:18:35.572 --> 00:18:38.617
I BELIEVE YOU/WHAT DOESN'T CHANGE

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:40.953
What did you want to talk about?

00:18:41.036 --> 00:18:46.959
Well, I think you've been giving Tasuku
money for living expenses,

00:18:47.918 --> 00:18:51.046
but have you talked to him
about the specifics of that?

00:18:51.713 --> 00:18:52.548
I have not.

00:18:53.757 --> 00:19:00.347
Is Tasuku really borrowing money
for the costs of living with you?

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:01.974
That is the case.

00:19:02.057 --> 00:19:05.144
What exactly are both of you
trying to say to me?

00:19:05.644 --> 00:19:07.271
How do we say this…?

00:19:07.813 --> 00:19:10.482
There is some reason for doubt here.

00:19:11.984 --> 00:19:12.985
It is fine.

00:19:13.777 --> 00:19:17.990
I believe in Sir Tasuku.
There are no problems.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:22.619
Furthermore, I…

00:19:27.082 --> 00:19:28.709
Are you Tasuku?

00:19:28.792 --> 00:19:31.128
Who are you?

00:19:31.211 --> 00:19:35.174
I'm Kobayashi, the lawyer who gives
Kotaro his living allowance.

00:19:35.257 --> 00:19:37.634
Ah, it's you. 'Sup!

00:19:37.718 --> 00:19:40.929
The money you've been collecting
to live with Kotaro,

00:19:41.722 --> 00:19:45.017
isn't it really for paying back your debt?

00:19:47.186 --> 00:19:51.648
What are you talking about, suddenly?
I would never do that. No.

00:19:51.732 --> 00:19:55.652
First of all, this has nothing to do
with you guys. It's between Kotaro and me.

00:19:55.736 --> 00:19:59.281
Hey, do you believe him?

00:19:59.364 --> 00:20:01.325
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:20:01.909 --> 00:20:05.078
I'm asking if you believe in him.

00:20:05.162 --> 00:20:07.497
What? I don't get what you're saying.

00:20:09.208 --> 00:20:11.460
He said he believes in you!

00:20:14.838 --> 00:20:16.340
Mr. Karino?

00:20:18.425 --> 00:20:20.010
What the heck? Damn it…

00:20:20.719 --> 00:20:23.347
Did they say something to Kotaro?

00:20:23.430 --> 00:20:24.431
Sir Tasuku!

00:20:24.973 --> 00:20:28.227
Oh! Hey, Kotaro. I just got here.

00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:30.938
By the way, were you
picking up garbage somewhere?

00:20:31.021 --> 00:20:32.439
That's awesome! Clean!

00:20:32.522 --> 00:20:35.234
It was nothing. It was for you, Tasuku.

00:20:35.317 --> 00:20:36.235
Hmm?

00:20:36.318 --> 00:20:39.154
Well, whatever.
Let's go to your room!

00:20:44.243 --> 00:20:46.578
Now, Sir Tasuku. Come on in.

00:20:46.662 --> 00:20:47.621
Thank you very much!

00:20:47.704 --> 00:20:49.665
Kotaro is going to end up--

00:20:49.748 --> 00:20:51.583
- I'm sorry, Ms. Kobayashi.
- Huh?

00:20:51.667 --> 00:20:53.502
Can you give him a little more time?

00:20:55.128 --> 00:20:56.838
If we make a move now,

00:20:57.464 --> 00:21:00.926
I feel like
we'll ruin his relationship with Tasuku.

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:05.222
I'd like to wait and see the outcome

00:21:05.931 --> 00:21:07.808
of him believing in Tasuku.

00:21:08.934 --> 00:21:10.269
Hey, Kotaro.

00:21:10.769 --> 00:21:13.480
Did your neighbor Karino and that lawyer

00:21:13.563 --> 00:21:15.440
say something about me?

00:21:15.524 --> 00:21:19.653
Yes. They probably wanted to tell me
that you are lying

00:21:19.736 --> 00:21:22.906
and stealing money from me.

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:24.324
I knew it!

00:21:24.408 --> 00:21:27.869
Haha. That can't be true. Right, Kotaro?

00:21:28.495 --> 00:21:31.999
No, you are lying to me right now,
are you not?

00:21:33.125 --> 00:21:34.668
What're you saying, Kotaro?

00:21:35.502 --> 00:21:37.421
Even before the two of them realized,

00:21:37.504 --> 00:21:40.257
I knew you were lying, Tasuku.

00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:42.259
What made you think that?

00:21:42.801 --> 00:21:45.304
I realized it when I saw your finger.

00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:50.434
Ever since we were in the orphanage,
when you lie,

00:21:50.517 --> 00:21:53.437
you fiddle with your pointer finger
on your left hand.

00:21:54.146 --> 00:21:57.691
It was like that
when you first came to see me.

00:22:00.694 --> 00:22:02.195
That's just a coincidence--

00:22:02.279 --> 00:22:06.116
I do not have an issue
with you lying, Sir Tasuku.

00:22:07.826 --> 00:22:10.787
This is the usual money. Take it.

00:22:12.873 --> 00:22:14.041
What is wrong?

00:22:15.709 --> 00:22:16.585
Why do this?

00:22:19.629 --> 00:22:21.757
I have a little favor to ask you.

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:23.467
I'm thinking about moving,

00:22:23.550 --> 00:22:25.510
but I don't have enough funds.

00:22:26.011 --> 00:22:28.472
So Kotaro, could you lend me some money?

00:22:28.555 --> 00:22:32.976
Then we can live together.
What do you think? Good plan, right?

00:22:34.853 --> 00:22:39.733
You think I'm lying about moving
and about us living together, right?

00:22:39.816 --> 00:22:41.860
So why are you giving me money?

00:22:42.652 --> 00:22:45.155
Do you remember, Sir Tasuku?

00:22:46.365 --> 00:22:50.202
When the wallet went missing,
you were suspected.

00:22:50.285 --> 00:22:53.080
I stood up for you that time.

00:22:53.705 --> 00:22:56.458
Now that you say it, that did happen.

00:22:56.958 --> 00:22:59.294
The wallet was safely found,

00:22:59.378 --> 00:23:01.588
but when I stood up for you,

00:23:01.671 --> 00:23:05.092
you told me, "You trust people too much."

00:23:05.592 --> 00:23:08.970
My words to you from back then

00:23:09.054 --> 00:23:10.514
still applies.

00:23:12.224 --> 00:23:15.519
Kotaro, you trust people too easily.

00:23:16.269 --> 00:23:20.107
Sir Tasuku, I believe you
because you are Sir Tasuku.

00:23:20.190 --> 00:23:21.233
Huh?

00:23:21.316 --> 00:23:24.778
If it is you,
I do not mind being betrayed.

00:23:24.861 --> 00:23:28.573
Even if you betray me,
I will still believe in you.

00:23:29.157 --> 00:23:31.660
No. I want to believe in you.

00:23:36.581 --> 00:23:39.751
And, Sir Tasuku, it's a little bit heavy,

00:23:39.835 --> 00:23:42.254
but take this
since I have prepared it for you.

00:23:42.337 --> 00:23:43.880
What? Coins?

00:23:43.964 --> 00:23:47.968
The money I have given you until now
is not mine.

00:23:48.051 --> 00:23:52.848
As I wanted to give you money that
I earned myself,

00:23:52.931 --> 00:23:55.142
I have been picking up cans.

00:23:57.519 --> 00:23:59.521
Why did you go that far?

00:23:59.604 --> 00:24:03.733
I was so happy that you said
you would live with me.

00:24:03.817 --> 00:24:06.736
But! That was a lie.

00:24:06.820 --> 00:24:08.697
I do not mind it being a lie!

00:24:09.197 --> 00:24:11.741
That is how happy it made me!

00:24:18.248 --> 00:24:20.041
When I left the orphanage,

00:24:20.125 --> 00:24:23.044
I tried to trust people like you, Kotaro.

00:24:23.879 --> 00:24:25.964
But I was betrayed so many times…

00:24:27.507 --> 00:24:29.843
Before I knew it, I ended up like this.

00:24:31.386 --> 00:24:32.471
I understand.

00:24:33.555 --> 00:24:38.143
It is painful not to be able to trust
someone who you want to trust.

00:24:43.732 --> 00:24:44.816
That's true.

00:24:46.067 --> 00:24:47.694
Sorry, Kotaro.

00:24:49.112 --> 00:24:51.531
Sorry and thank you.

00:25:00.332 --> 00:25:04.711
Tasuku quit being a host
and is working somewhere else now.

00:25:04.794 --> 00:25:08.423
It seems that he's paying Kotaro back
little by little too.

00:25:08.924 --> 00:25:10.133
I see.

00:25:10.717 --> 00:25:14.387
But why is he continuing to pick up cans?

00:25:18.600 --> 00:25:19.851
My thanks.

00:25:20.852 --> 00:25:22.854
Is this to prepare to live with Tasuku?

00:25:22.938 --> 00:25:27.317
Yes. Some day we will build a house
as big as a castle and live in it.

00:25:27.400 --> 00:25:30.737
Really? How commendable.

00:25:30.820 --> 00:25:32.364
You get jealous so easily.

00:25:32.447 --> 00:25:33.907
Huh? What do you mean?

00:25:34.449 --> 00:25:36.868
Sir Tasuku, Sir Ryota,

00:25:36.952 --> 00:25:39.788
Sir Karino, Lady Mizuki, Sir Tamaru,

00:25:39.871 --> 00:25:41.873
Lady Takei and Lady Kobayashi.

00:25:42.749 --> 00:25:44.334
There are still many more…

00:25:45.544 --> 00:25:49.798
I now have a dream!
To live together with all of you!

00:25:58.640 --> 00:26:01.851
Of course my father and mother
will both be with us!

00:26:03.645 --> 00:26:06.106
Tasuku, the sun will go down at that pace.

00:26:06.189 --> 00:26:09.859
I'm weak because
the cheek you punched hurts really bad.

00:26:09.943 --> 00:26:11.111
Did you say something?

00:26:11.194 --> 00:26:13.905
No, it was just a joke.

00:26:15.532 --> 00:26:17.701
You betrayed Kotaro.

00:26:17.784 --> 00:26:19.536
One punch isn't enough.

00:26:20.245 --> 00:26:22.914
I betrayed you too, Ryota.

00:26:22.998 --> 00:26:23.999
That's true.

00:26:24.082 --> 00:26:26.710
Even so, you referred me for this job.

00:26:26.793 --> 00:26:28.712
You're a goody-two-shoes human too, Ryota.

00:26:28.795 --> 00:26:30.005
Not really.

00:26:31.298 --> 00:26:33.883
There's no point in thinking about

00:26:33.967 --> 00:26:36.136
whether you'll betray us again or not.

00:26:36.928 --> 00:26:39.598
We'll just keep believing in you,

00:26:39.681 --> 00:26:41.016
both me and Kotaro.
